## How the pieces connect

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph IN[data/]
        CSV[5 supplied CSVs]
    end

    subgraph DB[MySQL: sql/setup.sql]
        RAW[raw tables<br/>player_profile · player_day<br/>purchase · currency_spend · ad_view]
        PC[purchase_clean<br/>duplicates removed<br/>refunds flagged]
        AL[ad_view_local<br/>timestamps −8h]
    end

    subgraph SQL[sql/01–05]
        DQ[01 data quality]
        P1[02–05 Part 1 metrics]
    end

    subgraph NB[notebooks/]
        N1[01 exploration<br/>Part 1]
        N2[02 deep dive<br/>Part 2]
        N3[03 channels<br/>Part 3]
        N4[04 churn<br/>Part 4]
    end

    subgraph OUT[readout/]
        FIG[figures/]
        DECK[Readout deck]
    end

    CSV --> RAW --> PC
    RAW --> AL
    RAW --> DQ
    PC --> P1
    AL --> P1
    P1 -->|run_sql_file| N1
    PC --> N2 & N3 & N4
    AL --> N2 & N4
    N1 & N2 & N3 & N4 --> FIG --> DECK
```

The notebooks run the queries in `sql/` directly through `run_sql_file()`, so the
Part 1 numbers in the notebooks and in the SQL come from the same code.

